# Kickstart Closeout Checklist

Use this checklist before transferring ownership to the team.

## Corpus baseline

- [ ] `doc/_meta/app-profile.yaml` reviewed or explicitly marked as incomplete.
- [ ] `doc/_meta/source-inventory.md` created.
- [ ] `doc/_meta/kickstart-report.md` created.
- [ ] `doc/CORPUS_MAP.md` still matches the actual corpus structure.
- [ ] Main indexes under `doc/_indexes/` initialized.
- [ ] Open questions recorded in `doc/_meta/open-questions.md`.

## Application understanding

- [ ] Main repository role identified: primary, secondary, library or unknown.
- [ ] Stack detected from evidence or marked as unknown.
- [ ] Main entry points identified when possible.
- [ ] At least the top application areas/features are listed.
- [ ] High-risk unknowns are visible.

## Production and operations

- [ ] Production knowledge status is explicit, even if empty.
- [ ] Known bugs, risks or incidents are captured when evidence exists.
- [ ] Observability sources are listed or marked unavailable.
- [ ] No production claim is presented as confirmed without evidence.

## Handover

- [ ] `HANDOVER_SUMMARY.md` completed.
- [ ] AI champion identified or explicitly unknown.
- [ ] `AI_CHAMPION_GUIDE.md` reviewed with the champion.
- [ ] `TEAM_USAGE_GUIDE.md` reviewed with the team.
- [ ] `NEXT_30_DAYS.md` adapted to the team context.
- [ ] `OPEN_DECISIONS.md` reviewed.
- [ ] `corpus-state.yaml` handover status updated.

## Exit criteria

The kickstart is complete when the team can explain:

- what the corpus currently knows;
- what remains uncertain;
- which agent to use for each common workflow;
- how to capture durable knowledge after real work.
